{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Like all the nations that are around me.</b> The reason for 'around me' is that the land of Israel is the central line below, and this is the sense of 'around me,' for all the lands surround it, in the manner of what is written (Ezekiel 5:5): ״זאת ירושלים בתוך הגוים שמתיה וסביבותיה ארצות״, and if so, Israel dwells among the seventy nations that encompass the earth, and from this he said, 'like all the nations that are around me.' And so David, peace be upon him, mentioned concerning this (Psalms 118:10): ״כל גוים סבבוני בשם ה' כי אמילם״. And this is the elevation of Israel and of the Holy Land as well, that they correspond to the central line above, which is the portion of Israel, which seventy princes encompass — from what they expounded: the Holy One, blessed be He, said to the seventy angels who surround the throne of His glory, 'Come, let us confound their language'; and so it is written (I Kings 22:19): ״ראיתי את ה' יושב על כסאו וכל צבא השמים עומדים עליו מימינו ומשמאלו״ — these are the seventy princes; these incline to the right to acquit and these incline to the left to condemn; and so it is further written (Psalms 89): ״ונורא על כל סביביו״. Therefore David, peace be upon him, explained and said that one should not trust in man known, nor in princes — who are the seventy princes of the nations — but in HaShem, who is the central line, their portion of Israel, and through Him he will cut them all off; and this is (ibid. 118): ״בשם ה' כי אמילם״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:05.040219205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}